tests:
  unit: { count: 345, covers: "Every rule at the level where it lives, 232 cases the epic adds or changes. THE STORE (W1): a written layout reads back unchanged; no dir, no file, non-JSON, a missing, extra or mistyped field read as no saved layout; a staged write never tears the file; the app bridge's null on refusal. THE SPLITTER (W3): ARIA separator, 8 / 48 px steps per axis and dir, Home/End, inert Enter, double-click reset, start-relative clamped drag with one commit per release, a press that never moves commits nothing, a lowered bound shown without a change, the short-leg minimum (DEC-68). THE BOUNDS (W3, W4): pane-min/pane-max/path-min/zone-min/zone-max and each col-* min/max read from the Tailwind tokens; splitter A's range matching the design run's identity at 1440/1311/1280/1132/850; the path track as minmax(path-min, 1fr); a wide column lowering listMin and the pane's max. THE HOOK (W3, W4): restore, clamp a stale value, whole-pixel widths, debounced write flushed on unmount, reset one and Reset Layout; columns.size renamed duration so an old file reads as none. THE MENU (W3): View > Reset Layout emits layout-reset in both builds. THE WINDOWS (W5): a saved rect placed against monitor sets (inside, gone, smaller, off an edge, below the minimum on 2x, straddling, none, frame, maximized); tracking moves and resizes only while normal; windows.json read whole or not at all. THE PIN (W6): the e2e workspace pins @wdio/tauri-service exactly and overrides no native-utils. At the close tip: core 366, shell 172, vitest 72 files / 60841 tests, all green." }
  integration: { count: 14, covers: "Each WU's bounded contract, 29 cases. layout_store.rs (W1): the wire fixture layoutWire.json, deserialised as the IPC delivers layout_write's argument, written into a temp config dir and read back equal - the snapshot-locked wire shape layoutStore.test.ts also reads. layoutSplit.test.tsx (W3): Layout and FlowDetail under one useLayout through a stubbed Tauri bridge - saved sizes restore, a key step and a whole drag each end in one layout_write, Reset Layout restores every default. layoutColumns.test.tsx (W4): Layout and FlowList under one useLayout - labels and rows open at the saved widths, a handle's step and drag write once, the pane's max follows the track sum. window_geometry_store.rs (W5): two labels saved, read back and placed against a two-monitor set return as saved; the file corrupted reads as no records. The xtask registry test: both shell builds register exactly the commands the app invokes." }
  e2e: { count: 9, covers: "THE EPIC'S FULL FLOW through the real Tauri window against a real ephemeral core (W6): cargo xtask ui e2e green, 7 of 7 spec files, 57 tests (layout 6 + 2 + 1). The list/pane split dragged past each end stops at 384 and the live maximum; the headers/body split saves 15 % and 60 %; the host column stops at 96 and 480 with path at least 128 and every label over its cells; arrows, Shift and Home/End step the splitter; double-click and Reset Layout (its layout-reset event, the native menu being out of WebDriver's reach) restore the defaults; pane, headers share, a column and the window size set, then a real quit - the relaunched app restores all four; a corrupt layout.json gives the defaults with no band and no warn notice. Both launchers remove layout.json and windows.json before and after a run. Off-monitor restore stays unit-level (W5): a second monitor is not hermetic." }
